1.	Install Python from https://www.python.org/.  I recommend the latest version supported by your computer’s Operating System (OS).  There are many great tutorials on YouTube if guided instruction is required.

2.	Install PyCharm from https://www.jetbrains.com/pycharm/.  PyCharm is an IDE purpose-built for Python and offers a comprehensive set of tools to enhance the Python coding experience.  Again, YouTube offers many tutorials for correctly downloading, installing, and configuring PyCharm.
